# AMQP access list of the local-cloud sysMonitor broker (RabbitMQ, topic exchange "arrowhead").
# A system is named here by the CN of its client certificate; scripts/generate-amqp-definitions.py turns it into the
# full subject of its system (sy) certificate, which the broker uses as user name (TLS EXTERNAL authentication, M1).
#   publish <routing-key pattern>    routing keys the system may publish with
#   subscribe <binding-key pattern>  binding keys the system may bind its own queues with
# Patterns use AMQP topic syntax: words separated by ".", "*" = one word, "#" = zero or more words.
# Routing keys: <Cloud>.sysmonitor.<System>.<serviceInstance>.<observationType>  (sysMonitor)
# After a change run "make amqp-acl": it regenerates amqp/definitions.json and loads it into the broker.

user RandomDataProducer.GoCloud.Company.arrowhead.eu
publish GoCloud.sysmonitor.RandomDataProducer.randomNumberProducer.#

user DataManager.GoCloud.Company.arrowhead.eu
publish GoCloud.sysmonitor.DataManager.DataManager.#

user TimeManager.GoCloud.Company.arrowhead.eu
publish GoCloud.sysmonitor.TimeManager.TimeManager.#

user Configuration.GoCloud.Company.arrowhead.eu
publish GoCloud.sysmonitor.Configuration.Configuration.#

user Choreographer.GoCloud.Company.arrowhead.eu
publish GoCloud.sysmonitor.Choreographer.Choreographer.#

user SysMonitor.GoCloud.Company.arrowhead.eu
subscribe GoCloud.sysmonitor.*.*.*
publish GoCloud.sysmonitor.SysMonitor.SysMonitor.*

